summed over $t \\in T$ and $1 \\le j \\le m$, from above by $x^{(e_D+e_L+3)\\varepsilon}\\mathcal B$ for an explicit quantity $\\mathcal B$, whose size \\ref{8JU6} estimates. Like the interval estimate itself, this is only an upper bound.","parent_id":105,"position":2}', 'claude');
